<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/bibliographicCitation> "Wexel, H. (2026). The Reprocessing System Ontology for a Circular Factory (Version 0.1.0). Collaborative Research Centre SFB 1574, Karlsruhe Institute of Technology. http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem" .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/created> "2026-10-14"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/creator> "Helena Wexel" .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "Funded by the Deutsche Forschungsgemeinschaft (DFG, German Research Foundation) - SFB 1574 - project ID 471687386."@en .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/license> <https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/> .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/modified> "2026-10-15"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date> .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/publisher> "Collaborative Research Centre SFB 1574 Circular Factory for the Perpetual Product, Karlsruhe Institute of Technology (KIT)"@en .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/title> "The Reprocessing System Ontology for a Circular Factory"@en .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespacePrefix> "rps" .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/preferredNamespaceUri> "http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem#" .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Domain ontology of SFB 1574 subproject C02 (Reprocessing System). Formerly drafted under the namespace https://w3id.org/circularfactory/C02#. It extends the Circular Factory Core Ontology with the resources, processes, operations, process parameters, in-process observations, monitoring datasets and data-driven models of the semi-autonomous additive-subtractive reprocessing of unique metallic components (high-speed DED-LB/M combined with machining) in the InRePro cell.\nReuse strategy: Core, SOSA and PROV-O are imported. QUDT is referenced but not imported because of its size; load the QUDT schema and the quantity-kind and unit vocabularies into the triple store separately. Terms of the Perpetual Product Ontology are referenced but not imported, because version 0.0.1 re-declares Core properties with conflicting domains and ranges. The alignment to DOLCE+DnS Ultralite is provided in the separate module reprocessing-system-dul-alignment.ttl.\nExtension point for causal knowledge (planned): process parameter settings (sosa:Actuation) and observations of deposit characteristics (sosa:Observation) are first-class individuals, so causal relations between them can be added later without changing existing terms."@en .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Reprocessing System Ontology"@en .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#versionInfo> "0.1.0" .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "OPEN ISSUE OI-1 (sensor and measurement classes): rps:Sensor and rps:Measurement are defined locally as specialisations of sosa:Sensor and sosa:Result, as recommended by INF, because it is not yet decided whether every CRC subproject needs cfc:Sensor and cfc:Measurement in the Core. If such classes are added to the Core, rps:Sensor and rps:Measurement are to be aligned to them or deprecated."@en .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "OPEN ISSUE OI-2 (uncertainty representation): the representation of measurement and prediction uncertainty (qudt:standardUncertainty, rps:hasCoverageFactor, rps:hasConfidenceLevel, rps:hasLowerPredictionBound, rps:hasUpperPredictionBound, rps:hasUncertaintyEvaluationMethod, rps:UncertaintyEvaluationMethod) is accepted by INF for now but must be aligned with the uncertainty models of subprojects B03 and A03."@en .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "OPEN ISSUE OI-3 (Core consistency): in Core 0.9.0, cfc:Component is unsatisfiable because cfc:hasOrigin has the two domains cfc:Assembly and cfc:Component, which are disjoint. This ontology follows the intended semantics (rps:ReprocessedComponent is a subclass of cfc:Component) and does not work around it. The modelling requirements of the Core are owned by A01; the correction is pending there."@en .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "OPEN ISSUE OI-4 (Perpetual Product Ontology): version 0.0.1 is referenced but not imported, because it re-declares Core properties with domains and ranges that conflict with Core 0.9.0 (e.g. cfc:hasFinalWorkpiece). To be imported once the two ontologies are harmonised."@en .
<http://w3id.org/circularfactory/ReprocessingSystem> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#editorialNote> "OPEN ISSUE OI-5 (further domain ontologies): an alignment to Onto3D was requested but not yet carried out because the intended ontology and namespace could not be identified unambiguously. QUDT is referenced but not imported because of its size."@en .
